# GD-20 (round 19, writer 10): L §4.2 Keys as values "a key of a year, month or day range `by n` with n above 1
# stands for its n periods (§4.1), so it is a period, never a law date: `at k` with k such a key is refused
# (LOAD-LAWPERIOD, §4.3)"; L §8.3 row `at <m>: a period is not a law date`. A week (a day range by 7).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index wk = day 2026-01-05..2026-12-28 by 7
input r: int
def d[w in wk]: int at w
  rule a = r

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 2

ask q: d[2026-01-05]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWPERIOD at w: a period is not a law date (m.tally:11)
